.TH "jags\-uninstall" "1" "" "Version 1.0" "JAGS Utilities User Manuals"
.SH NAME
jags\-uninstall \- remove installations of JAGS
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]jags\-uninstall\f[R] [\f[I]\-h\f[R]] [\f[I]\-c\f[R]]
[\f[I]\-o\f[R]] [\f[I]\-s\f[R]] [\f[I]\-d\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]jags\-uninstall\f[R] is a command\-line tool that can be used to
remove installations of JAGS (https://mcmc\-jags.sourceforge.io) created
by the official JAGS installers for macOS.
The default option removes \f[B]all\f[R] detected installations
including custom and legacy (version <= 4.x) builds in /usr/local/
and/or /opt/R/arm64 as well as official (version >= 5.x) builds under
/opt/jags.
To fine\-tune this behaviour see the available options below.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\-h\f[R]
Display a help message and exit.
.TP
\f[B]\-c\f[R]
Over\-ride the default and remove only custom/legacy JAGS installations
under /usr/local and/or /opt/R/arm64 (unless the \-o flag is also set).
.TP
\f[B]\-o\f[R]
Over\-ride the default and remove only official JAGS installations under
/opt/jags and (unless the \-c flag is also set) \- this option also
implies \-s.
.TP
\f[B]\-s\f[R]
Over\-ride the default and remove only symlinks under /usr/local that
point to /opt/jags/current (unless the \-o or \-c flag is also set).
.TP
\f[B]\-d\f[R]
Perform a dry\-run i.e.\ list the files/directories that would be
removed but don\[cq]t actually do anything.
